t. This means that the set does not span ${R}^{3}$ and therefore, cannot be a basis.\n\n- Statement “$\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$” is false. The set $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1}\\}$ is not a basis of ${R}^{3}$ because the set contains vectors from another vector space.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247104 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "055fd93a-dc3c-5837-bb7e-b10d2b5f586e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461611} {:answer/id #uuid "a80c3c5e-d9b4-5318-b1f6-d20a3da16b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "055fd93a-dc3c-5837-bb7e-b10d2b5f586e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461611} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2ae2459-61e0-5b34-a36e-84d3e8989367" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462559} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff5be9c2-3b47-5c46-95d5-045358b54872" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461613} {:answer/id #uuid "47ec3cb1-9a8d-5ae1-8405-a39633aac020" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47ec3cb1-9a8d-5ae1-8405-a39633aac020" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461614} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4ff86b1-edc5-53ff-a7db-1086daba7c30" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462560} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "630bb051-3efe-5a74-a086-01a568b3085a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461615} {:answer/id #uuid "c689ac4f-c64b-54da-8d4d-e1500110c4ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "630bb051-3efe-5a74-a086-01a568b3085a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461615} :answer-field/id #uuid "3af09c95-73be-5007-8368-88b917550558" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462561}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "11f8af48-def1-5000-8ab6-3793fdd8fd3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-110291" :question/problem "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an elementary matrix is obtained by performing exactly one elementary row operation on the identity matrix $I.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not an elementary matrix because it can't be obtained from $I$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from $I$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not an elementary matrix because it can't be obtained from $I$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\nTherefore, only $B$ is an elementary matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247105 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75fb586e-f579-51cf-bd9d-47ff1486b729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461617} {:answer/id #uuid "bdc11fdc-ce52-5c36-bad6-aca6df0112c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75fb586e-f579-51cf-bd9d-47ff1486b729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461617} :answer-field/id #uuid "57d8c5f5-4748-5d5e-b3fc-406fcb8ac660" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462562} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "201ce91a-f2af-5228-b077-e9c4dec01ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461619} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d897c7-655f-57c2-810f-6244cedbf59b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6d897c7-655f-57c2-810f-6244cedbf59b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461620} :answer-field/id #uuid "74e56853-cb78-585c-8cc8-8e2d2f6a89ae" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.typ